{"chapter": "desirables", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "02BK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{desirables-section-definition-algebraic-stacks}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:06181838789365fa83f47397584e66afdfe9a8cb30defddf4df93cc242a059e0", "source_text": "Definition of algebraic stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5443fb6a35e7456beaf30c5e66737c71338b4bba403800933646d87526a79a60", "unit_id": "tag:02BK:title"}
{"chapter": "desirables", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02BK", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-section-algebraic-stacks}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49778cfbfc1164c7ae6177de28bd3407cebf71c9e17e4317f504132feac247f1", "source_text": "An algebraic stack is a stack in groupoids over the category of schemes with the fppf topology that has a diagonal representable by algebraic spaces and is the target of a surjective smooth morphism from a scheme. See Algebraic Stacks, Section <REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a7f52ac7e7e9171c457f0b9e69147b5b50ba2af98c27b73b487e768753bf2ee7", "unit_id": "tag:02BK:p001"}
{"chapter": "desirables", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02BK", "placeholders": {"CITE_0001": "\\cite{DM}", "LATIN_0001": "\\'etale", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebraic-definition-deligne-mumford}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:41463fb32f58fc3e40334061ba88ffa5585080821347710c2981de08791b670f", "source_text": "A ``Deligne-Mumford stack'' is an algebraic stack for which there exists a scheme and a surjective <LATIN_0001> morphism from that scheme to it as in the paper <CITE_0001> of Deligne and Mumford, see Algebraic Stacks, Definition <REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ff4df69e6edbf87fcdcfad295ae71468f603d3839874e02379256faf7ac3bacb", "unit_id": "tag:02BK:p002"}
{"chapter": "desirables", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02BK", "placeholders": {"CITE_0001": "\\cite{ArtinI}", "CITE_0002": "\\cite{ArtinII}", "CITE_0003": "\\cite{ArtinVersal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b18a569a3bbf6d96bbb8bd4b3cd582f30925703ed16e4a23816c78853bf3ce05", "source_text": "We will reserve the term ``Artin stack'' for a stack such as in the papers by Artin, see <CITE_0001>, <CITE_0002>, and <CITE_0003>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8a9fc4ff925d2ec107a8844e78f6c5bf74e1a66d76d6b2ed5ee13afe83b6ecb0", "unit_id": "tag:02BK:p003"}
{"chapter": "desirables", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02BK", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{artin-section-axioms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:eabc450d370c03ffb592dc3328714b032619d73fa35edd358cf6a0d5759433d7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bf4a973598114e651570b5743a5efce7f7e8225788089b160d4aaef60c07c541", "source_text": "A possible definition is that an Artin stack is an algebraic stack <MATH_0001> over a locally Noetherian scheme <MATH_0002> such that <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>Namely, these are exactly the algebraic stacks over <MATH_0004> satisfying Artin's axioms [-1], [0], [1], [2], [3], [4], [5] of Artin's Axioms, Section <REF_0001>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b6ab42a8dc2786c9cc157764e51d869915b05dcc41c4cae0ad4281544b1c8c5", "unit_id": "tag:02BK:p004"}
